---
import baseline from "../../data/content-baseline.json";
import EquipmentVisual from "./EquipmentVisual.astro";
import SpecStrip from "./SpecStrip.astro";
import JobSiteCards from "./JobSiteCards.astro";
import MediaFigure from "./MediaFigure.astro";
import EquipmentFilm from "./EquipmentFilm.astro";
import ProcurementCtaTier from "./ProcurementCtaTier.astro";
const {locale="en"}=Astro.props;
const s=baseline.product.specifications;
---
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Portable light pole lifter</p><h1>Light pole lifting.<br/>Made portable.</h1><p class="lead muted">A two-module hydraulic system for road-lighting projects. Start with the pole, flange and foundation—then choose the configuration.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/products/light-pole-jack/">Explore the equipment <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/guides/pole-jack-compatibility/">Will it fit my project? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div><EquipmentVisual/></div>
    <SpecStrip/><p class="note"><span>Specification sheet data. Pole, flange, foundation and site compatibility require project review.</span> <span>Non-standard bases require a dimensioned drawing review.</span></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">The equipment</p><h2>Two modules.<br/>One project to review.</h2></div><p class="muted">The hydraulic lifting module and electrical cabinet form the system described in the product sheet. Review the dimensions, included components and connection details before selecting equipment.</p></div>
    <div class="two-column module-showcase"><div><MediaFigure src="/images/evidence/equipment-trolley-side-detail.jpg" alt="Close reference view of the hydraulic pump and wheeled lifting frame" label="01 / Hydraulic detail" caption="Equipment detail reference · Confirm the actual supplied components."/><div class="module-copy"><p class="section-number">01 / HYDRAULIC MODULE</p><h3>The lifting assembly</h3><p class="muted" style="margin-top:15px">Hydraulic cylinder, valve, oil pump and pressure gauge. The sheet lists a {s.hydraulicModuleWeightKg} kg module measuring {s.hydraulicModuleDimensionsMm.join(" × ")} mm.</p></div></div><div><MediaFigure src="/images/product/portable-pole-lifter-hero-cutout.png" alt="Lifting assembly beside its separate yellow electrical cabinet" label="02 / System overview" caption="Product reference · Hydraulic assembly and separate electrical cabinet." variant="cutout"/><div class="module-copy"><p class="section-number">02 / ELECTRICAL CABINET</p><h3>Power and control</h3><p class="muted" style="margin-top:15px">Control system, rechargeable {s.batteryVoltageV} V battery, ammeter, voltage meter and lift buttons. Cabinet dimensions: {s.electricalCabinetDimensionsMm.join(" × ")} mm.</p></div></div></div>
    <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:35px" href="/products/light-pole-jack/#specifications">See the complete specifications <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section film-section" id="equipment-overview"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">In focus / Equipment film</p><h2>A closer look.<br/>From frame to detail.</h2></div><p class="muted">Take a short visual tour of the equipment, hydraulic detail, connection and packing. Select a chapter to look closer.</p></div><EquipmentFilm locale={locale} id="home-equipment-film"/></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="background:#fff; border-top:1px solid var(--line); border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Application review / Reference images</p><h2>Different sites.<br/>Different questions to resolve.</h2></div><p class="muted">These images illustrate project contexts for review. They are not verified customer cases or proof of suitability; actual assemblies, access and foundations need assessment.</p></div><JobSiteCards limit={3}/></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="wrap two-column"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before the lift</p><h2>Height is only<br/>the starting point.</h2><p class="lead muted" style="margin-top:24px">A pole's assembled weight, flange, anchor bolts and foundation all matter. A matching height alone does not confirm compatibility.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/guides/pole-jack-compatibility/">Check the information you need <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="yellow-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Project review checklist</p><h3>Bring the drawing.<br/>Keep the assumptions out.</h3><ul><li>Pole height and assembled weight</li><li>Flange drawing and anchor bolt details</li><li>Foundation and site conditions</li><li>Quantity, application and destination</li></ul><p>Not sure about a dimension? Send what you have and identify what still needs confirmation.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A practical next step</p><h2>From specifications<br/>to your project.</h2></div><p class="muted">For electrical contractors, road-lighting teams and project procurement. Commercial terms are discussed privately after the application and configuration are reviewed.</p></div>
    <div class="step-row"><span>01</span><h3>Review the equipment</h3><p>Look at the rated load, module dimensions and standard included configuration. Distinguish source data from field results.</p></div>
    <div class="step-row"><span>02</span><h3>Collect the project details</h3><p>Use the compatibility guide to prepare the pole, flange and foundation information. Unknown details can be flagged for follow-up.</p></div>
    <div class="step-row"><span>03</span><h3>Request a configuration review</h3><p>Submit your details and optional drawing. A receipt reference confirms the inquiry has been recorded.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-top:40px"><ProcurementCtaTier locale={locale} highlightTier={1}/></div>
  </div></section>
</main>
<style>
  .module-showcase{gap:32px}.module-copy{padding-top:26px}.module-copy .section-number{margin-bottom:12px}.film-section{padding-top:0}
  @media(max-width:760px){.module-showcase{gap:40px}}
</style>
